# Widevine, the DRM module streaming apps play protected video with, when the user installed it
# (dsa drm widevine install). DSA ships none of Google's software: the host takes Google's
# com.google.android.widevine APEX, unchanged, out of Google's emulator system image of this
# Android version and architecture, and puts it on the user's add-on disk as widevine.img, an
# erofs image holding the APEX as its one file. The host adds androidboot.dsa.widevine=on to the
# boot's bootconfig only while that image is on the disk it attaches, with
# androidboot.dsa.widevine_image saying where to mount it from: "disk" for the file on the disk,
# or "dax" in the host's direct-mapped mode, where the partition table names the image's own
# bytes (dsa_widevine) on persistent memory.
#
# dsa-widevine-early.rc mounts the image and lays it over /vendor/apex at early-init, before
# apexd-bootstrap activates the APEXes there: make-image.py splices it into the system's init.rc,
# the one script read before this one. apexd checks the APEX's signature against the key it
# carries, as for the vendor's own, and mounts its payload with the labels Google's build gave
# its files, whose types the vendor policy declares (or sepolicy/widevine-hal.cil, where it does
# not): the module's service runs in hal_drm_widevine and keeps its device certificates in
# /data/vendor/mediadrm. This script keeps what happens once /data is there.

# The folder the module keeps its device certificates in, which Android's provisioning fills the
# first time an app uses Widevine.
on post-fs-data && property:ro.boot.dsa.widevine=on
    mkdir /data/vendor/mediadrm 0770 media mediadrm

# A boot after the user removed the module (androidboot.dsa.widevine=off) removes those
# certificates, so removing Widevine removes what it provisioned, and makes the folder again,
# empty, for any other DRM module. The vendor's toybox removes it, as root, in a domain that may
# touch nothing else (sepolicy/widevine.cil). A boot whose host says nothing either way (the
# host could not read its record) leaves it as it is.
on post-fs-data && property:ro.boot.dsa.widevine=off
    exec u:r:dsa_widevine_reset:s0 root root -- /vendor/bin/toybox_vendor rm -rf /data/vendor/mediadrm
    mkdir /data/vendor/mediadrm 0770 media mediadrm
    restorecon_recursive /data/vendor/mediadrm
